#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: [an] Through
#> pause: 45
#> must: [an] [an.*an] In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must: [an] Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
#> must: [\.] Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: [an] A stately
#> not: [an] Down
#> source: an.*an
# 5. Context addresses: which lines does a pattern select? McMahon 2.2-2.3
# The paper tests /an/ (lines 1, 3, 4), /an.*an/ (line 1 only: two "an"s with
# anything between), /^an/ (no line starts with "an") and /\./ (line 5, the
# only literal period). Each s below tags the lines its address selects.
# The /\./ test runs first so the tags added later cannot confuse it.
# Try: add /^an/s/^/[^an] / and see that it tags nothing; then try /^Wh/.
/\./s/^/[\\.] /
/an.*an/s/^/[an.*an] /
/an/s/^/[an] /

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
